                    AIController aiController = new AIController(camera);
Instantiation inside the GameBuilder, to should be more uniform (AI, and player has same initialisation)
Right now we have AiController  that need to have Camera in the constructor for moving unit to rally point from Barracks

and also a 	    // - Prepare user controller -
           		playerController.init(GP, CP, SB, GC, playerFaction, camera);

check the interface FactionController with 2 method overload (surcharge), AiController doesn't use .init() inside
the GameBuilder (and we should probably avoid using for PlayerController either.. )
Anyway refactor this later to find the most simple code structure (when we have a complete Ai behavior)




